Therefore, the Court dealing with an application under Section 34 of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act cannot meddle with the award it has to either accept the same or set aside the same;
(ii) When the circular itself was issued on 28.12.2017, the arbitral proceedings were pending before the District Collector/Land Acquisition Arbitrator.
Therefore, the appellants/respondents cannot be found fault for specifically not raising the issue in the claim petition;
Even if the person or an individual, over looks or unknowingly does not claim the benefit of a provision of grant of compensation where the State https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis exercises eminent domain and acquires the land, it cannot be heard to contend that by oversight the other person has not raised the issue and therefore, it will not pay the compensation.
The circular gives a right to seek for redetermination and not merely to attack the error in the original determination which is only the purpose of the arbitral proceedings.
